              <div class="result-item">
                <span class="result-label">Spot radius w<sub>0</sub></span>
                <span class="result-value" id="foc-out-w0">&mdash;</span>
              </div>
              <div class="result-item">
                <span class="result-label">Spot diameter 2w<sub>0</sub></span>
                <span class="result-value" id="foc-out-2w0">&mdash;</span>
              </div>
              <div class="result-item">
                <span class="result-label">Peak intensity</span>
                <span class="result-value" id="foc-out-I">&mdash;</span>
              </div>
              <div class="result-item">
                <span class="result-label">Peak fluence</span>
                <span class="result-value" id="foc-out-F">&mdash;</span>
              </div>
              <div class="result-item">
                <span class="result-label">Rayleigh range z<sub>R</sub></span>
                <span class="result-value" id="foc-out-zr">&mdash;</span>
              </div>
              <div class="result-item">
                <span class="result-label">Depth of focus 2z<sub>R</sub></span>
                <span class="result-value" id="foc-out-dof">&mdash;</span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="chart-wrap">
              <canvas id="foc-chart" aria-label="Focused beam profile and intensity"></canvas>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="notes-card card">
            <h4>Notes</h4>
            <p>
              <strong>Focus &amp; fluence.</strong> Focuses a collimated beam with a
              thin lens and reports the on-axis peak intensity and fluence of the
              resulting spot&nbsp;[1].
            </p>
            <div class="note-eq" {...eqAttrs} set:html={eq(String.raw`w_0=\frac{M^{2}\lambda f}{\pi w_{\mathrm{in}}},
              \qquad w_{\mathrm{in}}=\frac{\emptyset}{2},
              \qquad z_R=\frac{\pi w_0^{2}}{M^{2}\lambda}`)} />
            <div class="note-eq" {...eqAttrs} set:html={eq(String.raw`P_{\mathrm{peak}}=0.9394\,\frac{E}{\Delta t},
              \qquad I_{\mathrm{peak}}=\frac{2P_{\mathrm{peak}}}{\pi w_0^{2}},
              \qquad F_{\mathrm{peak}}=\frac{2E}{\pi w_0^{2}}`)} />
            <div set:html={defs([
              ['\\emptyset', '1/e&sup2; beam diameter before the lens'],
              ['f', 'focal length'],
              ['w_0', 'focused 1/e&sup2; spot radius'],
              ['E', 'pulse energy'],
              ['\\Delta t', 'intensity FWHM'],
              ['I_{\\mathrm{peak}}', 'on-axis intensity at the temporal peak'],
              ['F_{\\mathrm{peak}}', 'on-axis fluence (time-integrated)'],
            ])} />
            <p class="theory-note"><strong>Assumptions.</strong></p>
            <ul>
              <li>
                The input is collimated with its waist at a thin, aberration-free lens
                filled without clipping, and
                <span set:html={im('f\\ll z_{R,\\mathrm{in}}')} /> &mdash; which is what
                reduces the focusing law to the expression above.
              </li>
              <li>
                The factors of 2 make these the on-axis peak of a Gaussian profile:
                twice the <em>total</em> power (or energy) divided by the 1/e&sup2; area
                <span set:html={im('\\pi w_0^{2}')} />, inside which only
                <span set:html={im('1-e^{-2}=86.5\\%')} /> of the power actually lies.
              </li>
              <li>
                Both outputs are peak, not area-averaged, values &mdash; the mean
                intensity over that disc is
                <span set:html={im('0.432\\,I_{\\mathrm{peak}}')} />, not half of it
                &mdash; and both are quoted per cm&sup2;.
              </li>
              <li>
                <span set:html={im('P_{\\mathrm{peak}}')} /> uses the Gaussian shape
                factor here regardless of what the Peak&nbsp;Power tab is set to&nbsp;[3].
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- ============================================================ -->
      <!-- TAB 6: Chirp / Compressor                                     -->
      <!-- ============================================================ -->
      <div class="tab-panel" id="panel-chirp">
        <div class="widget-layout">
