            <div class="param-group">
              <span class="param-group__title">Transform limit</span>
              <div class="fields">
                <div class="field">
                  <label for="chirp-lam">&lambda;<sub>0</sub> (nm)</label>
                  <input type="text" class="field-input" id="chirp-lam" inputmode="decimal" value="800">
                </div>
                <div class="field">
                  <label for="chirp-dlam">&Delta;&lambda; (nm)</label>
                  <input type="text" class="field-input" id="chirp-dlam" inputmode="decimal" value="30">
                </div>
                <div class="field">
                  <label for="chirp-dtTL">&Delta;t<sub>TL</sub> (fs)</label>
                  <input type="text" class="field-input" id="chirp-dtTL" inputmode="decimal" readonly>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="param-group">
              <span class="param-group__title">Compressor material</span>
              <div class="fields">
                <div class="field">
                  <label for="chirp-mat">Material</label>
                  <select class="field-input" id="chirp-mat">
                    <option value="sio2">Fused silica</option>
                    <option value="bk7">BK7</option>
                    <option value="caf2">CaF&#8322;</option>
                    <option value="sapphire">Sapphire</option>
                    <option value="sf10">SF10</option>
                  </select>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

          </div>
          </ParamsDrawer>

          <div class="widget-column widget-column--results">
          <div class="results card">
            <h3>Results</h3>
            <div class="result-grid">
              <div class="result-item">
                <span class="result-label">Chirp ratio &Delta;t/&Delta;t<sub>TL</sub></span>
                <span class="result-value" id="chirp-out-ratio">&mdash;</span>
              </div>
              <div class="result-item">
                <span class="result-label">GDD on the pulse</span>
                <span class="result-value" id="chirp-out-gdd">&mdash;</span>
              </div>
              <div class="result-item">
                <span class="result-label">Compensating GDD</span>
                <span class="result-value" id="chirp-out-comp">&mdash;</span>
              </div>
              <div class="result-item">
                <span class="result-label">Material needed</span>
                <span class="result-value" id="chirp-out-mat">&mdash;</span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="chart-wrap">
              <canvas id="chirp-chart" aria-label="Pulse duration vs GDD"></canvas>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="notes-card card">
            <h4>Notes</h4>
            <p>
              <strong>Chirp &amp; compressor.</strong> Compares a measured duration with
              the transform limit implied by the spectrum, inverts the Gaussian
              broadening law for the residual GDD, and converts it into a thickness of
              glass&nbsp;[3,&nbsp;4].
            </p>
            <div class="note-eq" {...eqAttrs} set:html={eq(String.raw`\Delta t_{\mathrm{TL}}=\frac{K_{\mathrm{G}}}{\Delta\nu},
              \qquad \Delta\nu=\frac{c\,\Delta\lambda}{\lambda_0^{2}},
              \qquad K_{\mathrm{G}}=0.4413`)} />
            <div class="note-eq" {...eqAttrs} set:html={eq(String.raw`\mathrm{GDD}=\pm\,\frac{\Delta t_{\mathrm{TL}}^{2}}{4\ln 2}
              \sqrt{\left(\frac{\Delta t}{\Delta t_{\mathrm{TL}}}\right)^{\!2}-1}`)} />
            <div class="note-eq" {...eqAttrs} set:html={eq(String.raw`L=\frac{\left|\mathrm{GDD}\right|}{\left|\beta_2\right|}`)} />
            <div set:html={defs([
              ['\\Delta t', 'measured intensity FWHM'],
              ['\\Delta t_{\\mathrm{TL}}', 'transform-limited FWHM of the same spectrum'],
              ['\\Delta\\lambda', 'spectral FWHM'],
              ['\\mathrm{GDD}', 'group-delay dispersion carried by the pulse (fs&sup2;)'],
              ['\\beta_2', "the selected material's GVD at &lambda;<sub>0</sub>&nbsp;[6]"],
              ['L', 'thickness whose |GDD| matches'],
            ])} />
            <p class="theory-note"><strong>Assumptions.</strong></p>
            <ul>
              <li>
                A Gaussian pulse with pure second-order chirp &mdash; the Gaussian
                constant is used whatever shape the other tabs are set to, and
                <span set:html={im('\\Delta t\\ge\\Delta t_{\\mathrm{TL}}')} /> is required.
              </li>
              <li>
                Duration is an even function of GDD, so the sign cannot be recovered
                from <span set:html={im('\\Delta t')} /> alone: the readouts give the
                magnitude with both signs
                (<span set:html={im('\\pm')} />&nbsp;/&nbsp;<span set:html={im('\\mp')} />),
                and fixing the sign takes a phase-sensitive measurement&nbsp;[4].
              </li>
              <li>
                <span set:html={im('L')} /> uses
                <span set:html={im('\\left|\\beta_2\\right|')} />, so it is the thickness
                that <em>matches</em> the dispersion, not a claim that adding glass
                compresses the pulse.
              </li>
              <li>
                These materials have <span set:html={im('\\beta_2>0')} /> only below their
                zero-dispersion wavelength &mdash; roughly 1.27&nbsp;&micro;m for fused
                silica, 1.32&nbsp;&micro;m for BK7, 1.31&nbsp;&micro;m for sapphire,
                1.55&nbsp;&micro;m for CaF<sub>2</sub> and 1.71&nbsp;&micro;m for SF10.
                Above it <span set:html={im('\\beta_2<0')} />: the printed thickness is
                still positive, but that glass would <em>compress</em> a positively
                chirped pulse instead of stretching it, so removing positive chirp there
                needs a compressor rather than more glass.
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

