                  <label for="brt-frep">f<sub>rep</sub></label>
                  <div class="input-with-unit">
                    <input type="text" class="field-input" id="brt-frep" inputmode="decimal" value="160">
                    <select class="unit-sel" id="brt-frep-u">
                      <option value="1e3" selected>kHz</option>
                      <option value="1e6">MHz</option>
                      <option value="1">Hz</option>
                    </select>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="field">
                  <label for="brt-dt">&Delta;t (fs)</label>
                  <input type="text" class="field-input" id="brt-dt" inputmode="decimal" value="2">
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="param-group">
              <span class="param-group__title">Spectrum</span>
              <div class="fields">
                <div class="field">
                  <label for="brt-lam">&lambda;<sub>0</sub> (nm)</label>
                  <input type="text" class="field-input" id="brt-lam" inputmode="decimal" value="3000">
                </div>
                <div class="field">
                  <label for="brt-dlam">&Delta;&lambda; (nm)</label>
                  <input type="text" class="field-input" id="brt-dlam" inputmode="decimal" value="4000">
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="param-group">
              <span class="param-group__title">Beam quality</span>
              <div class="fields">
                <div class="field">
                  <label for="brt-w0">w<sub>0</sub> (&mu;m)</label>
                  <input type="text" class="field-input" id="brt-w0" inputmode="decimal" value="46">
                </div>
                <div class="field">
                  <label for="brt-M2">M&sup2;</label>
                  <input type="text" class="field-input" id="brt-M2" inputmode="decimal" value="1">
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

          </div>
          </ParamsDrawer>

          <div class="widget-column widget-column--results">
          <div class="results card">
            <h3>Results</h3>
            <div class="result-grid">
              <div class="result-item">
                <span class="result-label">Pulse energy</span>
                <span class="result-value" id="brt-out-energy">&mdash;</span>
              </div>
              <div class="result-item">
                <span class="result-label">Peak power</span>
                <span class="result-value" id="brt-out-ppeak">&mdash;</span>
              </div>
              <div class="result-item">
                <span class="result-label">Avg spectral density</span>
                <span class="result-value" id="brt-out-savg">&mdash;</span>
              </div>
              <div class="result-item">
                <span class="result-label">Peak spectral density</span>
                <span class="result-value" id="brt-out-speak">&mdash;</span>
              </div>
              <div class="result-item">
                <span class="result-label">Avg spectral brightness</span>
                <span class="result-value" id="brt-out-bavg">&mdash;</span>
              </div>
              <div class="result-item">
                <span class="result-label">Peak spectral brightness</span>
                <span class="result-value" id="brt-out-bpeak">&mdash;</span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="chart-wrap">
              <canvas id="brt-chart" aria-label="Brightness comparison"></canvas>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="notes-card card">
            <h4>Notes</h4>
            <p>
              <strong>Spectral brightness.</strong> Turns the power, spectrum and beam
              quality of a laser source into photon brightness (brilliance) in a
              1/e&sup2; area-times-solid-angle convention &mdash; within a numerical
              factor of the phase-space convention used for synchrotron brilliance, so a
              table-top source can be put on the same axis as a large facility.
            </p>
            <div class="note-eq" {...eqAttrs} set:html={eq(String.raw`A\Omega=\left(\pi w_0^{2}\right)
              \left(\pi\theta^{2}\right)=M^{4}\lambda_0^{2},
              \qquad \theta=\frac{M^{2}\lambda_0}{\pi w_0}`)} />
            <div class="note-eq" {...eqAttrs} set:html={eq(String.raw`S=\frac{P}{\Delta\lambda},
              \qquad P_{\mathrm{peak}}=0.9394\,\frac{P_{\mathrm{avg}}}{f_{\mathrm{rep}}\,\Delta t},
              \qquad P\in\left\{P_{\mathrm{avg}},\ P_{\mathrm{peak}}\right\}`)} />
            <div class="note-eq" {...eqAttrs} set:html={eq(String.raw`B=\frac{P}{A\Omega}\cdot
              \frac{10^{-3}\lambda_0}{\Delta\lambda}\cdot\frac{\lambda_0}{hc}\cdot 10^{-12}`)} />
            <div set:html={defs([
              ['A\\Omega', 'area&ndash;solid-angle product (&eacute;tendue) of the beam, in m&sup2;&middot;sr'],
              ['\\lambda_0,\\ \\Delta\\lambda', 'centre wavelength and spectral FWHM'],
              ['S', 'spectral power density, reported in W per nm of bandwidth for both the average and the peak power'],
              ['M^{2}', 'beam-quality factor, the same in both transverse directions'],
              ['hc/\\lambda_0', 'photon energy at the centre wavelength'],
              ['10^{-3}\\lambda_0/\\Delta\\lambda', 'the fraction of the power inside a 0.1% bandwidth'],
              ['10^{-12}', 'converts m&sup2;&middot;sr to mm&sup2;&middot;mrad&sup2;'],
              ['B', 'photons per second per mm&sup2; per mrad&sup2; per 0.1% bandwidth'],
            ])} />
            <p class="theory-note"><strong>Assumptions.</strong></p>
            <ul>
              <li>
                The waist cancels out of <span set:html={im('A\\Omega')} />, so
                <span set:html={im('w_0')} /> only has to be a sensible nonzero number
                &mdash; brightness is set by <span set:html={im('M^{2}')} /> and
                <span set:html={im('\\lambda_0')} /> alone&nbsp;[1,&nbsp;2].
              </li>
              <li>
                The 0.1%-bandwidth slice assumes a <em>flat</em> spectral density over
                <span set:html={im('\\Delta\\lambda')} />, which for the multi-octave
                default spectrum is a rough approximation, and the photon energy is
                taken at <span set:html={im('\\lambda_0')} /> for the whole band.
              </li>
              <li>
                The synchrotron figure of merit is built from rms phase-space areas,
                which for a diffraction-limited beam give
                <span set:html={im('A\\Omega=\\lambda_0^{2}/4')} /> &mdash; four times
                smaller than the 1/e&sup2; product used here, so the bar for your source
                sits about 0.6&nbsp;decades below a brilliance quoted in that convention.
              </li>
              <li>
                Average brightness uses the time-averaged power, peak brightness the
                within-pulse peak with the Gaussian shape factor.
              </li>
              <li>
                The defaults loaded here are the multi-octave source of&nbsp;[7].
              </li>
              <li>
                The four comparison bars (thermal lamp, third-generation synchrotron,
                table-top HHG, XFEL) are order-of-magnitude markers for orientation
                only, not sourced measurements of any particular facility.
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- ============================================================ -->
      <!-- TAB 9: Beam Modes (LG/HG)                                    -->
      <!-- ============================================================ -->
      <div class="tab-panel" id="panel-modes">
        <div class="widget-layout">
          <ParamsDrawer>
          <div class="controls card">
            <h3>Beam Modes</h3>

            <div class="param-group">
              <span class="param-group__title">Mode family</span>
              <div class="shape-row" id="modes-family">
                <button class="preset-btn active" data-shape="lg">Laguerre-Gauss</button>
                <button class="preset-btn" data-shape="hg">Hermite-Gauss</button>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="param-group" id="modes-lg-params">
              <span class="param-group__title">LG indices</span>
              <div class="fields">
                <div class="field">
                  <label for="modes-l">&ell; (azimuthal)</label>
                  <input type="text" class="field-input" id="modes-l" inputmode="decimal" value="1">
                </div>
                <div class="field">
                  <label for="modes-p">p (radial)</label>
                  <input type="text" class="field-input" id="modes-p" inputmode="decimal" value="0">
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="param-group" id="modes-hg-params" style="display:none">
              <span class="param-group__title">HG indices</span>
              <div class="fields">
                <div class="field">
                  <label for="modes-m">m (horizontal)</label>
                  <input type="text" class="field-input" id="modes-m" inputmode="decimal" value="2">
                </div>
                <div class="field">
                  <label for="modes-n">n (vertical)</label>
                  <input type="text" class="field-input" id="modes-n" inputmode="decimal" value="1">
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="param-group">
              <span class="param-group__title">Beam</span>
              <div class="fields">
                <div class="field">
                  <label for="modes-w0">w<sub>0</sub> (&mu;m)</label>
                  <input type="text" class="field-input" id="modes-w0" inputmode="decimal" value="100">
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

          </div>
          </ParamsDrawer>

          <div class="widget-column widget-column--results">
          <div class="results card">
            <h3>Intensity profile</h3>
            <div class="result-grid">
              <div class="result-item">
                <span class="result-label">Mode label</span>
                <span class="result-value" id="modes-out-label">&mdash;</span>
              </div>
              <div class="result-item">
                <span class="result-label">OAM per photon</span>
                <span class="result-value" id="modes-out-oam">&mdash;</span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="chart-wrap">
              <canvas id="modes-chart" aria-label="Beam mode intensity profile"></canvas>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="notes-card card">
            <h4>Notes</h4>
            <p>
              <strong>Beam modes.</strong> Draws the transverse intensity pattern of a
              free-space Laguerre&ndash;Gauss or Hermite&ndash;Gauss mode at its
              waist&nbsp;[1].
            </p>
            <div id="modes-note-math">
              <div data-family="lg">
                <div class="note-eq" {...eqAttrs} set:html={eq(String.raw`I_{\ell,p}(r)\propto
                  \left(\frac{2r^{2}}{w_0^{2}}\right)^{\!\left|\ell\right|}
                  \left[L_p^{\left|\ell\right|}\!\!\left(\frac{2r^{2}}{w_0^{2}}\right)\right]^{2}
                  \exp\!\left(-\frac{2r^{2}}{w_0^{2}}\right)`)} />
                <div set:html={defs([
                  ['r', 'radius from the axis'],
                  ['w_0', '1/e&sup2; waist radius of the fundamental mode'],
                  ['\\ell', 'azimuthal index; the mode carries &ell;&hbar; of orbital angular momentum per photon'],
                  ['p', 'radial index, giving p radial nodes'],
                  ['L_p^{\\left|\\ell\\right|}', 'generalised Laguerre polynomial'],
                ])} />
              </div>
              <div data-family="hg" hidden>
                <div class="note-eq" {...eqAttrs} set:html={eq(String.raw`I_{m,n}(x,y)\propto
                  H_m^{2}\!\!\left(\frac{\sqrt{2}\,x}{w_0}\right)
                  H_n^{2}\!\!\left(\frac{\sqrt{2}\,y}{w_0}\right)
                  \exp\!\left(-\frac{2\left(x^{2}+y^{2}\right)}{w_0^{2}}\right)`)} />
                <div set:html={defs([
                  ['x,\\ y', 'Cartesian transverse coordinates'],
                  ['w_0', '1/e&sup2; waist radius of the fundamental mode'],
                  ['m,\\ n', 'horizontal and vertical indices, giving m and n nodal lines'],
                  ['H_m', 'Hermite polynomial (physicists&rsquo; convention)'],
                ])} />
              </div>
            </div>
            <p id="modes-note">
              <strong>LG<sub>1,0</sub>.</strong> Donut mode with 1&#8463; OAM. Central
              null from phase singularity.
            </p>
            <p class="theory-note"><strong>Assumptions.</strong></p>
            <ul>
              <li>
                The profile is taken at the waist (<span set:html={im('z=0')} />), so
                there is no Gouy phase, curvature or <span set:html={im('z')} /> scaling.
              </li>
              <li>
                The azimuthal phase <span set:html={im('e^{i\\ell\\varphi}')} /> that
                carries the angular momentum is not drawn, only
                <span set:html={im('\\left|E\\right|^{2}')} />.
              </li>
              <li>
                The map spans <span set:html={im('\\pm 3w_0')} /> in units of the waist
                and is normalised to its own maximum, so the pattern is identical for
                every <span set:html={im('w_0')} /> &mdash; the waist only sets the
                physical width printed under the map.
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Examples — below the result box, aligned to the result-box width (as in the Mie scattering lab) -->
      <div class="examples-row" id="examples-row">
        <PresetStrip presets={laserPresets} showCopy={false} />
      </div>

      <div class="references card">
        <h4>References</h4>
        <ul class="reference-list">
          <li><span class="ref-index">[1]</span><span>A. E. Siegman, <em>Lasers</em> (University Science Books, 1986).</span></li>
          <li><span class="ref-index">[2]</span><span>ISO 11146-1:2021, <em>Lasers and laser-related equipment &mdash; Test methods for laser beam widths, divergence angles and beam propagation ratios &mdash; Part 1: Stigmatic and simple astigmatic beams</em> (ISO, 2021).</span></li>
          <li><span class="ref-index">[3]</span><span>J.-C. Diels &amp; W. Rudolph, <em>Ultrashort Laser Pulse Phenomena</em>, 2nd ed. (Academic Press, 2006).</span></li>
          <li><span class="ref-index">[4]</span><span>R. Trebino, <em>Frequency-Resolved Optical Gating: The Measurement of Ultrashort Laser Pulses</em> (Kluwer Academic, 2000).</span></li>
          <li><span class="ref-index">[5]</span><span>R. W. Boyd, <em>Nonlinear Optics</em>, 4th ed. (Academic Press, 2020).</span></li>
          <li><span class="ref-index">[6]</span><span>Sellmeier coefficients: I. H. Malitson, <em>Interspecimen comparison of the refractive index of fused silica</em>, J. Opt. Soc. Am. <strong>55</strong>, 1205 (1965), <a href="https://doi.org/10.1364/JOSA.55.001205" target="_blank" rel="noopener">doi:10.1364/JOSA.55.001205</a>; I. H. Malitson, <em>A redetermination of some optical properties of calcium fluoride</em>, Appl. Opt. <strong>2</strong>, 1103 (1963), <a href="https://doi.org/10.1364/AO.2.001103" target="_blank" rel="noopener">doi:10.1364/AO.2.001103</a>; I. H. Malitson &amp; M. J. Dodge, J. Opt. Soc. Am. <strong>62</strong>, 1405 (1972) (sapphire); SCHOTT optical glass catalogue (N-BK7, SF10).</span></li>
          <li><span class="ref-index">[7]</span><span>U. Elu, L. Maidment, L. Vamos, F. Tani, D. Novoa, M. H. Frosz, V. Badikov, D. Badikov, V. Petrov, P. St. J. Russell &amp; J. Biegert, <em>Seven-octave high-brightness and carrier-envelope-phase-stable light source</em>, Nature Photonics <strong>15</strong>, 277&ndash;280 (2021), <a href="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41566-020-00735-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener">doi:10.1038/s41566-020-00735-1</a>.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
<script>
import { initPermalinks } from '../../lib/permalink';
initPermalinks({
